// optional 0x80 R/B swap) drawn in order over one 16-byte block (four pixels) of one row. Each thread is one block: its group X
// (r0.1) and row Y (r0.6) from the walker, at the pixel x = px0 + 4 X and y = py0 + Y (CURBE dwords 1 and 2; CURBE dword 0 is
// the record count; CURBE dword 3 is the low 32 bits of the image surface base on binding table entry 2).
//
// Binding table entry 0 is the destination surface (read once at entry, written back once at exit). Binding table entry 1 is the
// records (count of them, 32 bytes each, two per 64-byte row, pitch 64: record k at x = 32 (k & 1), row k >> 1). Binding table
// entry 2 is the linear image surface (16384 bytes a row, byte offset B at x = B & 16383, y = B >> 14, as gpu_i915_scale.iga).
